Ansible Tags: Run Only What You Need

In Ansible, tags help you control which parts of a playbook to execute, saving time and resources during deployments.

Imagine you have a large playbook that does many things – installs software, configures services, etc. Sometimes, you only want to run a specific part of it, perhaps just the configuration tasks or only the package installations.

That's where tags come in! 

You can label individual tasks (or even entire plays) in your Ansible playbook with descriptive tags.
This allows for much more targeted automation, saving time and resources when you don't need to run the entire playbook. It's like having fine-grained control over your automation!

Tip: Use meaningful tag names and avoid over-tagging.
